Chapter: FramelessLeafProbe

 Reduction for ARM64 frame elision on plain leaves.

 Every leaf below is call-free by the gate's own analysis: bit-and,
 bit-or, bit-xor, bit-shl and bit-shru are on a64-is-known-inline, so
 a64-body-has-non-tail-call answers False for these bodies. But the
 ARM64 runtime records functions NAMED bit-and, bit-or, bit-xor,
 bit-shl and bit-shru (Arm64Runtime.codex, a64-record-func), and
 a64-emit-direct-call prefers a recorded function over the inline arm
 for any known builtin, so each of these "inline" operations is in
 fact emitted as a BL to the two-instruction runtime helper. Framed,
 that BL is harmless. Frameless there is no saved LR, so the first BL
 destroys x30 and the leaf's RET can never leave the function again.

 Under the current gate (a64-can-be-frameless requires a64-should-tco)
 all five leaves are emitted FRAMED and this probe passes. Under the
 reverted widened gate (plain call-free leaves admitted) flp-add32,
 flp-rotl32 and flp-gmul2 go frameless with a BL inside; flp-plusk
 goes frameless with a BL to the zero-arg constant flp-mask (the bare
 IrName arm of a64-emit-name is also a call the analysis cannot see).
 flp-block is the control: a pure compare-and-literal chain with no
 bit ops and no named constants, deep enough to walk the frameless
 local file into x19 if the nested-if result locals overflow.

Section: Leaves

  flp-add32 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  flp-add32 (a) (b) = bit-and (a + b) 4294967295

  flp-rotl32 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  flp-rotl32 (val) (n) =
    let masked = bit-and val 4294967295
    in bit-and (bit-or (bit-shl masked n) (bit-shru masked (32 - n))) 4294967295

  flp-gmul2 : Integer -> Integer
  flp-gmul2 (a) =
    if a >= 128 then bit-xor (bit-and (bit-shl a 1) 255) 27
    else bit-and (bit-shl a 1) 255

  flp-block : Integer -> Integer
  flp-block (cp) =
    let v = cp - 128
    in if v < 256 then 0
    else if v < 384 then 1
    else if v < 512 then 2
    else if v < 640 then 3
    else if v < 768 then 4
    else if v < 896 then 5
    else if v < 1024 then 6
    else if v < 1152 then 7
    else if v < 1664 then 8
    else if v < 1920 then 9
    else if v < 2048 then 10
    else 0 - 1

  flp-mask : Integer = 4294967295

  flp-plusk : Integer -> Integer
  flp-plusk (x) = x + flp-mask

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("add32=" & show (flp-add32 1634760805 2036477234))
    print-line-uni ("rotl32=" & show (flp-rotl32 1634760805 7))
    print-line-uni ("gmul2=" & show (flp-gmul2 202))
    print-line-uni ("block=" & show (flp-block 628))
    print-line-uni ("plusk=" & show (flp-plusk 7))
  end
